+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ygDj1HC1VxvK36nMfyCk6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n2\t\n3\tImplement the core of the task queue: the ability to add tasks and retrieve them in first-in, first-out order.\n4\t\n5\t## Requirements\n6\t\n7\t- The queue should accept a payload (any data) when a task is added, and return a task object.\n8\t- Each task must have a unique identifier (e.g., UUID), a status, and a creation timestamp.\n9\t- New tasks start in a \"pending\" state.\n10\t- Retrieving the next task should return the oldest pending task and transition it to a \"processing\" state.\n11\t- If no tasks are available, retrieval should return `null`.\n12\t- There should be a way to check how many tasks are waiting.\n13\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9863f08a-9aa8-4f19-afb8-b8dc6c2021ba","uuid":"c6f27129-e6ff-4437-aee9-24bfd89e25db","timestamp":"2026-05-31T00:40:54.011Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-01.md","content":"# Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n\nImplement the core of the task queue: the ability to add tasks and retrieve them in first-in, first-out order.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- The queue should accept a payload (any data) when a task is added, and return a task object.\n- Each task must have a unique identifier (e.g., UUID), a status, and a creation timestamp.\n- New tasks start in a \"pending\" state.\n- Retrieving the next task should return the oldest pending task and transition it to a \"processing\" state.\n- If no tasks are available, retrieval should return `null`.\n- There should be a way to check how many tasks are waiting.\n","numLines":13,"startLine":1,"totalLines":13}}}
